1
00:00:15,329 --> 00:00:17,330
HA JUNG-WOO

2
00:00:17,331 --> 00:00:19,333
IM SOO-JUNG

3
00:00:22,836 --> 00:00:25,005
KIM JUN-HAN

4
00:00:25,505 --> 00:00:27,257
KRYSTAL JUNG

5
00:00:33,597 --> 00:00:35,599
SHIM EUN-KYUNG

6
00:00:54,534 --> 00:00:58,955
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

7
00:00:59,790 --> 00:01:00,706
7TH NATIONAL CHILDREN'S
WRITING CONTEST

8
00:01:00,707 --> 00:01:03,376
The Grand Prize winner of
the National Children's Writing Contest

9
00:01:03,377 --> 00:01:04,753
FALL 1999
came from our school.

10
00:01:05,712 --> 00:01:10,592
Let's welcome the proud winner
Jeon Yi-gyeong with applause!

11
00:01:35,450 --> 00:01:37,494
I don't have a dad.

12
00:01:38,203 --> 00:01:40,414
Other kids have dads,

13
00:01:40,747 --> 00:01:43,291
but there's just me
and my mom at our home.

14
00:01:44,501 --> 00:01:45,751
However,

15
00:01:45,752 --> 00:01:48,505
my mom is stronger than all the dads.

16
00:01:49,881 --> 00:01:51,216
Our house is big.

17
00:01:52,008 --> 00:01:54,802
There's a huge chandelier
in the living room.

18
00:01:54,803 --> 00:01:58,432
Mom always walks with
the click-clack sound of her heels.

19
00:01:59,766 --> 00:02:03,311
If there are no flowers at home,
Mom doesn't go out.

20
00:02:04,229 --> 00:02:07,232
She always brings home
lilies or hydrangeas.

21
00:02:08,066 --> 00:02:09,401
Mom says,

22
00:02:09,943 --> 00:02:13,113
"A home is a person's face.
It must not be messy."

23
00:02:14,239 --> 00:02:15,907
My mom is very cool.

24
00:02:16,908 --> 00:02:19,118
Yi-gyeong, you could become a writer.

25
00:02:19,119 --> 00:02:20,954
You write even better than me.

26
00:02:21,204 --> 00:02:24,708
If you read books every day like me,
you can write well too.

27
00:02:27,461 --> 00:02:29,670
Why say you have no dad?

28
00:02:29,671 --> 00:02:31,423
Is that something to brag about?

29
00:02:31,757 --> 00:02:33,800
Hey, she got an award.
Why say that?

30
00:02:34,134 --> 00:02:36,343
Just write for fun.

31
00:02:36,344 --> 00:02:38,305
Don't even dream of being a writer.

32
00:02:39,222 --> 00:02:41,183
It's just a job for beggars.

33
00:02:42,934 --> 00:02:43,977
Okay, smile!

34
00:02:44,728 --> 00:02:45,353
Smile.

35
00:02:45,771 --> 00:02:47,773
One, two, three!

36
00:02:49,232 --> 00:02:50,442
Okay, let's take one more.

37
00:02:51,151 --> 00:02:53,570
One, two, three!

38
00:03:34,569 --> 00:03:40,158
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

39
00:03:42,118 --> 00:03:45,455
EPISODE 6

40
00:03:51,962 --> 00:03:54,880
Abduction,
murder in a vegetative state...

41
00:03:54,881 --> 00:03:56,007
What's with this family?

42
00:03:56,508 --> 00:03:57,592
Should we do a ritual?

43
00:03:59,803 --> 00:04:01,680
EVIDENCE 3

44
00:04:02,097 --> 00:04:02,930
That's the weapon, right?

45
00:04:02,931 --> 00:04:03,473
Yes

46
00:04:09,062 --> 00:04:10,355
- Bo-ram.
- Yes?

47
00:04:10,939 --> 00:04:11,898
Stand right there.

48
00:04:15,527 --> 00:04:16,945
She got hit

49
00:04:18,154 --> 00:04:20,574
right after she went in.

50
00:04:22,701 --> 00:04:23,869
She just fell over.

51
00:04:24,870 --> 00:04:26,872
And then she was struck again.

52
00:04:33,128 --> 00:04:33,837
What about the landlord?

53
00:04:34,045 --> 00:04:35,796
He's outside right now.

54
00:04:35,797 --> 00:04:36,548
Let's go.

55
00:04:41,136 --> 00:04:42,053
We're seeing each other quite often.

56
00:04:42,971 --> 00:04:43,930
Yes.

57
00:04:45,223 --> 00:04:48,268
I heard you found the body this morning.

58
00:04:48,685 --> 00:04:49,310
Yes.

59
00:04:49,311 --> 00:04:50,437
What time was it?

60
00:04:51,646 --> 00:04:53,565
I think around 7 to 7:30?

61
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:56,859
Why did Ms. Jeon come in here?

62
00:04:56,860 --> 00:04:58,069
Do you have any guesses?

63
00:05:00,030 --> 00:05:01,114
Not really.

64
00:05:01,573 --> 00:05:04,116
It's just a simple question,

65
00:05:04,117 --> 00:05:05,660
so no need to worry.

66
00:05:06,411 --> 00:05:08,871
If needed,
a formal investigation will be done.

67
00:05:08,872 --> 00:05:09,705
Okay.

68
00:05:09,706 --> 00:05:11,499
Are we suspects?

69
00:05:11,958 --> 00:05:14,127
Well, right now,
everyone is a suspect.

70
00:05:15,045 --> 00:05:17,130
Oh, I guess that makes sense.

71
00:05:17,589 --> 00:05:18,547
Right.

72
00:05:18,548 --> 00:05:19,799
It will come out
in the investigation.

73
00:05:20,133 --> 00:05:20,967
You have CCTV, right?

74
00:05:21,217 --> 00:05:22,009
Yes.

75
00:05:22,010 --> 00:05:23,803
- May we take a look?
- Sure.

76
00:05:45,867 --> 00:05:47,202
Is this all you have?

77
00:05:48,578 --> 00:05:49,412
Yes.

78
00:05:50,121 --> 00:05:51,039
Why?

79
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:55,960
Oh, we started using
the CCTV last night.

80
00:05:55,961 --> 00:05:58,380
It was off due to issues before that.

81
00:05:59,047 --> 00:06:00,631
You haven't been using it

82
00:06:00,632 --> 00:06:03,259
and happened to start using it last night?

83
00:06:03,551 --> 00:06:05,135
Yes.

84
00:06:05,136 --> 00:06:06,137
It worked out well.

85
00:06:06,596 --> 00:06:08,098
Thanks to that, the culprit was recorded.

86
00:06:11,935 --> 00:06:13,436
The only entrance
is over there, right?

87
00:06:14,145 --> 00:06:14,771
Yes.

88
00:06:16,898 --> 00:06:18,400
And that's the cafe owner?

89
00:06:19,150 --> 00:06:21,403
I heard the cafe owner
hasn't been seen for days.

90
00:06:24,739 --> 00:06:26,490
Yes, you're right.

91
00:06:26,491 --> 00:06:27,742
Only his part-time workers.

92
00:06:31,037 --> 00:06:31,830
What's wrong?

93
00:06:32,122 --> 00:06:34,332
Doesn't this situation seem strange?

94
00:06:36,835 --> 00:06:38,086
What's strange about it?

95
00:06:39,295 --> 00:06:41,297
The things only happening
in this building.

96
00:06:41,589 --> 00:06:43,883
Hmm, I'm not sure.

97
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:51,391
Mom! Mom!

98
00:06:53,393 --> 00:06:54,268
Ms. Jeon, just a moment!

99
00:06:54,269 --> 00:06:55,019
Let go!

100
00:06:55,020 --> 00:06:55,978
Ms. Jeon!

101
00:06:55,979 --> 00:06:57,146
Mom!

102
00:06:57,147 --> 00:06:59,523
- Mom!
- Yi-gyeong!

103
00:06:59,524 --> 00:07:00,734
Get a hold of yourself.

104
00:07:02,235 --> 00:07:04,362
Seon...

105
00:07:05,071 --> 00:07:07,197
My mom.

106
00:07:07,198 --> 00:07:09,534
Why is my mom here?

107
00:07:11,077 --> 00:07:13,163
Why is my mom here?

108
00:08:48,007 --> 00:08:49,008
Yi-gyeong.

109
00:08:56,057 --> 00:08:59,184
Oh my! Yi-gyeong!

110
00:08:59,185 --> 00:09:00,145
Yi-gyeong, wake up!

111
00:09:00,937 --> 00:09:01,938
Oh no.

112
00:09:02,438 --> 00:09:03,231
Are you okay, Yi-gyeong?

113
00:09:15,869 --> 00:09:17,537
Yi-gyeong, are you okay?

114
00:09:21,332 --> 00:09:22,500
Seon...

115
00:09:23,418 --> 00:09:24,627
How did I...

116
00:09:26,129 --> 00:09:27,172
Don't you remember?

117
00:09:27,881 --> 00:09:29,174
You collapsed.

118
00:09:35,138 --> 00:09:37,390
Su-jong is preparing the funeral,

119
00:09:38,433 --> 00:09:39,517
so there's no rush.

120
00:09:40,435 --> 00:09:41,644
Just lie down and rest.

121
00:09:42,061 --> 00:09:42,896
Seon.

122
00:09:44,647 --> 00:09:45,940
That storage room...

123
00:09:47,650 --> 00:09:48,526
Storage room?

124
00:09:48,776 --> 00:09:50,653
The basement storage
in your building.

125
00:09:53,406 --> 00:09:54,908
Oh, that place?

126
00:09:56,034 --> 00:09:56,868
What about it?

127
00:09:58,661 --> 00:10:00,538
I was just wondering
if it was there before.

128
00:10:02,332 --> 00:10:03,291
Oh.

129
00:10:04,042 --> 00:10:05,167
Well,

130
00:10:05,168 --> 00:10:07,669
it used to be a storage freezer,
but it broke down.

131
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:10,757
Now, we just use it
as a storage room for junk.

132
00:10:11,883 --> 00:10:12,926
Why do you ask?

133
00:10:18,014 --> 00:10:19,932
Can you help me up?

134
00:10:19,933 --> 00:10:20,934
Oh, sure.

135
00:10:22,060 --> 00:10:23,394
No, I'll lift you up.

136
00:10:24,270 --> 00:10:25,938
Ms. Jeon Yi-gyeong?

137
00:10:25,939 --> 00:10:26,856
Oh.

138
00:10:28,858 --> 00:10:30,525
You need to stay calm.

139
00:10:30,526 --> 00:10:31,569
I'm fine.

140
00:10:31,986 --> 00:10:34,280
Oh, hold on.
Let me explain first.

141
00:10:34,697 --> 00:10:36,741
So, did you know?

142
00:10:38,201 --> 00:10:39,369
About my mom's situation?

143
00:10:39,869 --> 00:10:41,996
No, not that incident.

144
00:10:46,542 --> 00:10:48,211
You're pregnant.

145
00:10:49,462 --> 00:10:50,255
What?

146
00:10:51,506 --> 00:10:52,715
W-Who?

147
00:10:53,258 --> 00:10:56,261
You fainted,
so we did a routine blood test and...

148
00:11:00,348 --> 00:11:02,100
Is it definite?

149
00:11:04,352 --> 00:11:06,687
I've notified the obstetrics
and gynecology department.

150
00:11:06,688 --> 00:11:08,230
The rounds will be here soon.

151
00:11:08,231 --> 00:11:09,691
- Take care.
- Yes.

152
00:11:30,128 --> 00:11:31,087
Yi-gyeong.

153
00:11:33,506 --> 00:11:35,008
You should eat something.

154
00:11:36,009 --> 00:11:37,135
Think about the baby.

155
00:11:44,267 --> 00:11:45,143
What's wrong?

156
00:11:45,852 --> 00:11:47,312
It's sour.

157
00:12:45,078 --> 00:12:46,329
Mister.

158
00:13:09,268 --> 00:13:11,103
I can't believe this.

159
00:13:11,104 --> 00:13:12,938
How could this happen?

160
00:13:12,939 --> 00:13:16,067
Just the day before,
she was doing fine. What happened?

161
00:13:16,692 --> 00:13:17,777
Thanks for coming.

162
00:13:18,403 --> 00:13:19,612
Yi-gyeong, you have a visitor.

163
00:13:43,386 --> 00:13:43,885
Your mother...

164
00:13:43,886 --> 00:13:45,012
I met your mother before.

165
00:13:45,805 --> 00:13:47,140
Nam Sang-ho, Policy Advisor
at Seoul City Urban Planning Committee

166
00:13:47,849 --> 00:13:48,640
I see...

167
00:13:48,641 --> 00:13:49,766
I pray

168
00:13:49,767 --> 00:13:52,019
she finds peace in a comfortable place.

169
00:13:54,939 --> 00:13:56,190
- This way.
- Sure.

170
00:13:59,819 --> 00:14:01,612
Nam Sang-ho, Policy Advisor
at Seoul City Urban Planning Committee

171
00:14:04,657 --> 00:14:05,949
Mr. Nam.

172
00:14:05,950 --> 00:14:07,952
- Oh?
- Yes.

173
00:14:10,121 --> 00:14:11,205
Please have a seat over there.

174
00:14:12,206 --> 00:14:14,000
Oh, it's been a while.

175
00:14:14,625 --> 00:14:17,086
Let me pour you a drink.

176
00:14:33,811 --> 00:14:35,354
Do you hang out with this kind of guy?

177
00:14:38,608 --> 00:14:40,443
That's a bit harsh, don't you think?

178
00:14:55,500 --> 00:14:58,336
So, Mr. Gi,
have you thought about it?

179
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:00,462
Yes.

180
00:15:00,463 --> 00:15:02,797
I'm going to ride in the same boat as you.

181
00:15:02,798 --> 00:15:05,301
You made the right decision.

182
00:15:06,594 --> 00:15:09,514
By the way,
do you know that old man well?

183
00:15:12,016 --> 00:15:13,643
We actually have a Go club
in our building.

184
00:15:14,018 --> 00:15:15,853
He's a tenant there.
I see him every day.

185
00:15:16,229 --> 00:15:20,565
Oh, then that guy must know
the Han-maum building very well.

186
00:15:20,566 --> 00:15:21,359
Yes.

187
00:15:21,901 --> 00:15:22,693
How about it?

188
00:15:23,194 --> 00:15:25,112
Can you buy it?

189
00:15:26,864 --> 00:15:29,533
If you bring
that building to me,

190
00:15:29,534 --> 00:15:31,953
I can give you 10% more.

191
00:15:33,454 --> 00:15:35,581
Oh, that would be 10 billion, right?

192
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:40,962
Depending on dividends,
the amount could go up.

193
00:15:42,421 --> 00:15:43,464
Let's eat.

194
00:15:47,969 --> 00:15:49,554
Oh!

195
00:15:50,263 --> 00:15:51,471
Have you eaten?

196
00:15:51,472 --> 00:15:53,640
Yes,
all the food is delicious.

197
00:15:53,641 --> 00:15:56,226
It's not easy to make good food
at a funeral home.

198
00:15:56,227 --> 00:15:57,186
What about the culprit?

199
00:15:57,770 --> 00:15:58,771
Oh...

200
00:15:59,480 --> 00:16:00,648
You see,

201
00:16:01,107 --> 00:16:02,983
given the current situation,

202
00:16:02,984 --> 00:16:06,152
the cafe owner, Oh Dong-ki,
is definitely the culprit.

203
00:16:06,153 --> 00:16:07,445
Hmm.

204
00:16:07,446 --> 00:16:09,574
We've issued a wanted notice,
so he'll be caught soon.

205
00:16:10,992 --> 00:16:12,367
And earlier,

206
00:16:12,368 --> 00:16:13,868
when I was kidnapped,

207
00:16:13,869 --> 00:16:17,707
didn't you mention something
about the place I was held?

208
00:16:18,624 --> 00:16:19,750
What do you mean?

209
00:16:22,003 --> 00:16:22,877
Coffee grounds.

210
00:16:22,878 --> 00:16:23,671
What?

211
00:16:23,838 --> 00:16:26,172
Coffee grounds were on her clothes.

212
00:16:26,173 --> 00:16:28,426
Oh, that's right.
It's matches up.

213
00:16:28,634 --> 00:16:30,218
Wait, so that means

214
00:16:30,219 --> 00:16:32,430
the cafe owner is the kidnapper.

215
00:16:33,139 --> 00:16:34,348
Wow.

216
00:16:35,308 --> 00:16:37,476
Is this crime connected like that? Huh?

217
00:16:42,106 --> 00:16:43,065
Hey, where are you going?

218
00:16:47,153 --> 00:16:48,571
Mr. Nam Sang-ho?

219
00:16:51,073 --> 00:16:51,907
Yes?

220
00:16:52,408 --> 00:16:54,869
I called for the witness survey,
but you did not respond.

221
00:16:55,536 --> 00:16:57,704
Oh, that police officer?

222
00:16:57,705 --> 00:17:00,416
Hold on, where did you say you worked for?

223
00:17:00,666 --> 00:17:02,501
I'm Koh Ju-ran
from the Yongdaemun Crime Unit.

224
00:17:03,628 --> 00:17:06,255
You knew the recently deceased
Jung Chang-su, right?

225
00:17:07,923 --> 00:17:09,008
Jung Chang-su?

226
00:17:11,302 --> 00:17:14,055
We found your business card
on his dead body.

227
00:17:18,768 --> 00:17:20,435
I mean, is there anyone

228
00:17:20,436 --> 00:17:22,438
without my card in this field?

229
00:17:22,938 --> 00:17:25,691
My card is practically like a flyer.

230
00:17:26,275 --> 00:17:28,026
Mr. Gi, don't you have my business card?

231
00:17:28,027 --> 00:17:29,069
I have mine right here.

232
00:17:29,070 --> 00:17:30,820
Hey! Get back here!

233
00:17:30,821 --> 00:17:32,572
Oh, I'm sorry.

234
00:17:32,573 --> 00:17:33,615
She just gets a bit too eager.

235
00:17:33,616 --> 00:17:35,409
It's fine.

236
00:17:40,206 --> 00:17:41,624
Jeez...

237
00:17:43,334 --> 00:17:44,542
- Honey.
- Yes?

238
00:17:44,543 --> 00:17:45,502
Do you need anything?

239
00:17:45,503 --> 00:17:46,878
- No, I'm fine.
- Okay.

240
00:17:46,879 --> 00:17:48,797
I'll bring the food over.

241
00:17:48,798 --> 00:17:49,548
Sure.

242
00:17:51,676 --> 00:17:53,135
She's pretty bold.

243
00:17:54,637 --> 00:17:57,223
Do young people these days
have no manners like that?

244
00:18:00,267 --> 00:18:03,019
Anyway, Mr. Gi,

245
00:18:03,020 --> 00:18:04,938
I want you to bring
that old man's building.

246
00:18:04,939 --> 00:18:05,648
Got it?

247
00:18:06,399 --> 00:18:07,692
- Yes.
- Okay.

248
00:18:09,235 --> 00:18:10,527
- I'll get going.
- Oh, sure.

249
00:18:10,528 --> 00:18:11,820
No, you don't
have to walk me out.

250
00:18:11,821 --> 00:18:12,697
Good day.

251
00:18:13,906 --> 00:18:15,115
Yes.

252
00:18:15,116 --> 00:18:15,740
I'm heading out.

253
00:18:15,741 --> 00:18:17,910
Yes, take care.

254
00:18:24,625 --> 00:18:25,835
Jeez.

255
00:18:28,754 --> 00:18:29,755
You said you didn't know, right?

256
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:32,216
What?

257
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:34,175
Nam Sang-ho.

258
00:18:34,176 --> 00:18:35,720
Do you know an advisor
named Nam Sang-ho?

259
00:18:36,137 --> 00:18:37,012
No.

260
00:18:37,388 --> 00:18:38,472
Who is this guy?

261
00:18:54,905 --> 00:18:56,991
LET'S GO TO OUR BUILDING

262
00:19:03,038 --> 00:19:05,124
RIGHT NOW? DON'T WE NEED TO STAY HERE?

263
00:19:12,506 --> 00:19:14,967
The police are suspecting Oh Dong-ki.
What if they check the restroom?

264
00:19:25,144 --> 00:19:26,520
GOT IT

265
00:19:32,902 --> 00:19:35,571
Yi-gyeong asked
about the storage freezer?

266
00:19:35,905 --> 00:19:36,739
Yes.

267
00:19:47,958 --> 00:19:49,210
All done. This was the last one.

268
00:19:52,797 --> 00:19:55,508
What exactly were they saying?
Do they suspect me or...

269
00:19:55,966 --> 00:19:56,884
Or what?

270
00:19:57,301 --> 00:19:59,386
I guess you could
suspect Oh Dong-ki.

271
00:20:00,221 --> 00:20:02,347
I don't know about that.

272
00:20:02,348 --> 00:20:05,643
It didn't seem like that,
but I think she knows something.

273
00:20:08,020 --> 00:20:08,938
Let's think about it.

274
00:20:10,314 --> 00:20:13,400
I mean, it's clear that Oh Dong-ki
is the criminal right now.

275
00:20:13,943 --> 00:20:14,777
Right.

276
00:20:16,237 --> 00:20:18,405
But what if he gets caught?

277
00:20:18,948 --> 00:20:20,783
If he gets caught,
he'll talk about us.

278
00:20:21,408 --> 00:20:22,909
- That's true.
- Of course.

279
00:20:22,910 --> 00:20:24,619
Then he absolutely can't get caught.

280
00:20:24,620 --> 00:20:25,829
No way. Not now.

281
00:20:25,830 --> 00:20:26,664
Right.

282
00:20:29,124 --> 00:20:30,166
Don't we need

283
00:20:30,167 --> 00:20:31,876
to put Oh Dong-ki
on a smuggling boat or something?

284
00:20:31,877 --> 00:20:33,169
Oh, that scared me.

285
00:20:33,170 --> 00:20:34,088
Hold on a second.

286
00:20:37,383 --> 00:20:38,133
What's this?

287
00:20:39,301 --> 00:20:40,636
Just answer it.

288
00:20:43,430 --> 00:20:44,223
Hello?

289
00:20:44,515 --> 00:20:45,558
It's your fault.

290
00:20:48,310 --> 00:20:49,603
Yes, Dong-ki.

291
00:21:01,031 --> 00:21:01,949
Who's there?

292
00:21:03,242 --> 00:21:04,326
It's me. Seyoon Building.

293
00:21:08,497 --> 00:21:10,790
No one's following you, right?

294
00:21:10,791 --> 00:21:11,542
No.

295
00:21:17,172 --> 00:21:18,007
Oh, right.

296
00:21:18,382 --> 00:21:19,674
You're not bugged, are you?

297
00:21:19,675 --> 00:21:21,467
Come on, why would we be?

298
00:21:21,468 --> 00:21:23,720
If we tell the police,
we'll be in big trouble.

299
00:21:23,721 --> 00:21:24,805
Come in.

300
00:21:31,103 --> 00:21:32,854
Oh, I think it smells here.

301
00:21:32,855 --> 00:21:34,857
Do you mind if we ventilate a bit?

302
00:21:43,032 --> 00:21:44,158
What are you doing right now?

303
00:21:44,575 --> 00:21:45,659
Oh!

304
00:21:47,036 --> 00:21:49,495
Just open the window.
Were you sending some signal out there?

305
00:21:49,496 --> 00:21:51,290
Come on. What signal?

306
00:21:54,376 --> 00:21:55,419
What's with the suit?

307
00:21:55,753 --> 00:21:56,794
Oh,

308
00:21:56,795 --> 00:21:58,004
we just came back from the funeral home.

309
00:21:58,005 --> 00:21:59,547
For the person you killed.

310
00:21:59,548 --> 00:22:00,757
Are you blaming me now?

311
00:22:00,758 --> 00:22:02,426
No, I just answered the question
because you asked.

312
00:22:04,345 --> 00:22:05,429
Anyway, what about the money?

313
00:22:06,138 --> 00:22:07,138
Well, you see...

314
00:22:07,139 --> 00:22:10,266
The police are all over the place,

315
00:22:10,267 --> 00:22:11,517
so we couldn't take out the money.

316
00:22:11,518 --> 00:22:13,519
That's your problem!

317
00:22:13,520 --> 00:22:16,606
Bring me the money, okay?
Before I blow this whole thing up!

318
00:22:16,607 --> 00:22:18,442
Dong-ki,
lower your voice right now.

319
00:22:20,194 --> 00:22:23,029
Just give us a bit more time.

320
00:22:23,030 --> 00:22:23,864
How much time?

321
00:22:24,031 --> 00:22:24,822
One week.

322
00:22:24,823 --> 00:22:26,616
Let's just all die, okay?

323
00:22:26,617 --> 00:22:27,700
Let's die then.

324
00:22:27,701 --> 00:22:28,993
Okay, okay.

325
00:22:28,994 --> 00:22:30,371
I'll get it ready as fast as I can.

326
00:22:30,788 --> 00:22:31,538
Understood?

327
00:22:32,665 --> 00:22:33,958
It's two billion.

328
00:22:34,583 --> 00:22:35,584
But you said one billion?

329
00:22:43,509 --> 00:22:45,176
If you made me suffer like this,

330
00:22:45,177 --> 00:22:46,303
you should at least double it.

331
00:22:51,058 --> 00:22:53,352
But did you treat that hand?

332
00:22:53,602 --> 00:22:55,104
If you leave it, it'll get worse.

333
00:22:57,064 --> 00:22:58,107
Dong-ki.

334
00:22:58,607 --> 00:23:01,819
once you do get the money,

335
00:23:02,611 --> 00:23:03,779
do you have any plans?

336
00:23:04,738 --> 00:23:06,115
I'll handle it myself!

337
00:23:06,657 --> 00:23:08,075
Are you confident
you won't get caught?

338
00:23:08,867 --> 00:23:11,829
Are you scared
I'll get arrested or something?

339
00:23:12,579 --> 00:23:13,956
Of course, I trust you.

340
00:23:15,249 --> 00:23:16,458
Remember that video?

341
00:23:17,042 --> 00:23:18,335
We're a team now.

342
00:23:18,502 --> 00:23:20,087
Get out with that nonsense.

343
00:23:22,756 --> 00:23:25,134
Hey, don't think about
messing with me.

344
00:23:25,676 --> 00:23:26,593
Gosh.

345
00:23:40,899 --> 00:23:42,568
Let's pay him. Set a date.

346
00:23:46,613 --> 00:23:48,072
- What are you doing?
- Huh?

347
00:23:48,073 --> 00:23:48,824
What?

348
00:23:48,949 --> 00:23:51,702
What were you thinking?
You're distracted right now.

349
00:23:53,704 --> 00:23:54,747
You know,

350
00:23:55,748 --> 00:23:59,083
the person who was with me
at that lady's funeral?

351
00:23:59,084 --> 00:24:00,668
Mr. Nam, that policy advisor.

352
00:24:00,669 --> 00:24:01,503
And?

353
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,005
He said something

354
00:24:04,298 --> 00:24:06,466
about the redevelopment.

355
00:24:06,467 --> 00:24:09,595
If we take over Mr. Kim's building,
we're going to hit it big.

356
00:24:11,555 --> 00:24:13,598
But what about Oh Dong-ki?

357
00:24:13,599 --> 00:24:15,225
What are you talking about?

358
00:24:15,434 --> 00:24:17,727
I've decided to join
the redevelopment investment company

359
00:24:17,728 --> 00:24:20,147
that Mr. Nam is working for.

360
00:24:20,564 --> 00:24:22,732
It's completely 100% confirmed.

361
00:24:22,733 --> 00:24:23,900
There's no risk involved.

362
00:24:23,901 --> 00:24:25,860
The returns are over 1,000%.

363
00:24:25,861 --> 00:24:28,947
So you're saying you want to
buy a building without paying Oh Dong-ki?

364
00:24:29,198 --> 00:24:30,157
Are you out of your mind?

365
00:24:30,657 --> 00:24:32,701
So if we pay Oh Dong-ki,
everything will be fine?

366
00:24:33,077 --> 00:24:35,328
What if that guy takes the money
and then blackmails us again?

367
00:24:35,329 --> 00:24:37,497
But he said he would
blow things up if we don't pay him.

368
00:24:37,498 --> 00:24:39,540
Then are you going to bury Oh Dong-ki?

369
00:24:39,541 --> 00:24:40,876
Is that what you want?

370
00:24:41,210 --> 00:24:44,003
I'm just saying
we're discussing this right now.

371
00:24:44,004 --> 00:24:45,672
This opportunity is too good to miss.

372
00:24:46,507 --> 00:24:48,674
This isn't an opportunity,
it's a crisis!

373
00:24:48,675 --> 00:24:51,011
If we mess up, our family is done for!

374
00:24:56,975 --> 00:24:58,184
You say

375
00:24:58,185 --> 00:25:00,437
it's for family,
but all you care about is yourself.

376
00:25:00,854 --> 00:25:02,356
What are you going to do about Da-rae?

377
00:25:03,607 --> 00:25:04,733
Just give up.

378
00:25:05,317 --> 00:25:07,778
It's not like the money we have
is honest anyway.

379
00:25:08,946 --> 00:25:10,322
Let's live within our means.

380
00:25:19,164 --> 00:25:21,834
Ju-ran, is there any point
in us hiding out here?

381
00:25:22,501 --> 00:25:24,044
Will Oh Dong-ki come back here?

382
00:25:24,753 --> 00:25:26,713
Maybe he hid some cash
or something.

383
00:25:28,340 --> 00:25:30,050
But doesn't
something feel a bit off?

384
00:25:30,968 --> 00:25:32,677
I mean, Ms. Jeon is one thing.

385
00:25:32,678 --> 00:25:34,471
But why was Oh Dong-ki in the basement?

386
00:25:35,889 --> 00:25:36,974
It does seem strange.

387
00:25:38,433 --> 00:25:39,852
So I thought about it.

388
00:25:40,352 --> 00:25:41,561
Oh Dong-ki was

389
00:25:41,562 --> 00:25:43,897
trapped in the storage freezer.

390
00:25:44,398 --> 00:25:45,731
Then when the door opened,

391
00:25:45,732 --> 00:25:47,651
he tried to escape and just attacked.

392
00:25:48,569 --> 00:25:49,778
Who locked him up?

393
00:25:50,154 --> 00:25:51,071
The landlord.

394
00:25:52,489 --> 00:25:53,657
Do you think so too?

395
00:25:54,241 --> 00:25:55,449
A while ago,

396
00:25:55,450 --> 00:25:58,036
when you suspected Gi Su-jong,
I wondered why.

397
00:25:58,537 --> 00:26:01,039
But now, with all these things
that keep happening around him...

398
00:26:02,916 --> 00:26:04,668
But why did Gi Su-jong
keep the tenant locked up?

399
00:26:06,044 --> 00:26:07,004
Exactly.

400
00:26:09,590 --> 00:26:11,758
I find that puzzling too.

401
00:26:23,520 --> 00:26:26,273
Do you remember the person you saw
at Ms. Jeon's funeral?

402
00:26:26,523 --> 00:26:27,441
Nam Sang-ho.

403
00:26:27,858 --> 00:26:28,858
Nam Sang-ho?

404
00:26:28,859 --> 00:26:29,735
Who's that?

405
00:26:33,530 --> 00:26:34,573
What happened?

406
00:26:35,324 --> 00:26:36,700
You said you took care
of the accident, right?

407
00:26:39,494 --> 00:26:43,248
My business card was found
on Jung Chang-su's body.

408
00:26:44,082 --> 00:26:44,875
Well?

409
00:26:45,334 --> 00:26:47,628
Is killing people all you guys do?

410
00:26:48,003 --> 00:26:49,128
In that case,

411
00:26:49,129 --> 00:26:51,173
just go out and spread rumors everywhere.

412
00:26:52,966 --> 00:26:53,967
I'm sorry.

413
00:26:55,636 --> 00:26:57,762
You go through all this
and then get insulted.

414
00:26:57,763 --> 00:26:59,932
Does it feel good or bad?

415
00:27:00,265 --> 00:27:01,225
But you see,

416
00:27:01,850 --> 00:27:03,477
there's a reason for it.

417
00:27:04,269 --> 00:27:06,229
Your brains

418
00:27:06,230 --> 00:27:07,522
are not cut out for this.

419
00:27:08,148 --> 00:27:09,857
You work hard

420
00:27:09,858 --> 00:27:11,108
but can't get a regular job.

421
00:27:11,109 --> 00:27:12,319
So when are you going to make money?

422
00:27:12,611 --> 00:27:15,239
Should I call Real Capital HQ?

423
00:27:15,656 --> 00:27:18,242
Are these kids really useless?

424
00:27:19,284 --> 00:27:22,579
I'll make sure
to avoid this mistake next time.

425
00:27:29,836 --> 00:27:32,965
You should have
done better earlier.

426
00:27:34,967 --> 00:27:36,051
Hurry to the hospital.

427
00:27:37,010 --> 00:27:39,512
- Thank you.
- You're bleeding.

428
00:27:39,513 --> 00:27:40,389
Go.

429
00:27:41,556 --> 00:27:43,267
- I'm sorry.
- Yes, hurry up and go.

430
00:27:48,230 --> 00:27:49,856
Should I just
go in and kill him?

431
00:27:54,778 --> 00:27:56,571
That wouldn't be fun.

432
00:27:58,365 --> 00:28:00,450
Sorry. I'll see you tomorrow.

433
00:28:08,041 --> 00:28:09,751
What a carefree guy.

434
00:28:11,670 --> 00:28:12,879
Do you want to have a drink too?

435
00:28:16,925 --> 00:28:18,218
Hwal-sung.

436
00:28:18,844 --> 00:28:20,137
What do you think?

437
00:28:21,305 --> 00:28:24,849
Do you want me to give up too?

438
00:28:24,850 --> 00:28:25,767
Speak up.

439
00:28:29,104 --> 00:28:31,690
If you hadn't made that suggestion
back then,

440
00:28:33,275 --> 00:28:34,735
we wouldn't be in this situation.

441
00:28:35,986 --> 00:28:37,111
What should I do now?

442
00:28:37,112 --> 00:28:38,113
What should I do?

443
00:28:41,074 --> 00:28:44,077
Hey, why did you do that with Seon?

444
00:28:44,995 --> 00:28:48,040
You betrayed your friend and your wife?

445
00:28:48,665 --> 00:28:49,750
Is that fun?

446
00:28:51,543 --> 00:28:53,503
You don't know
Yi-gyeong is pregnant, do you?

447
00:28:54,338 --> 00:28:55,964
Yi-gyeong is pregnant.

448
00:28:58,759 --> 00:28:59,718
Bastard.

449
00:29:01,178 --> 00:29:03,388
You're not even human.

450
00:29:10,896 --> 00:29:11,938
What about you?

451
00:29:14,232 --> 00:29:15,192
Hwal-sung.

452
00:29:15,817 --> 00:29:16,568
Are you okay?

453
00:29:20,572 --> 00:29:21,698
Tell me.

454
00:29:22,866 --> 00:29:24,701
What kind of person are you?

455
00:29:26,870 --> 00:29:28,622
What do you mean? Are you okay?

456
00:29:29,706 --> 00:29:30,874
Want me to tell you?

457
00:29:34,127 --> 00:29:37,839
Seon told me when we slept together.

458
00:29:39,508 --> 00:29:40,425
You have

459
00:29:42,803 --> 00:29:44,471
no confidence.

460
00:29:46,098 --> 00:29:48,475
You're just a worthless poor beggar,

461
00:29:49,643 --> 00:29:51,770
so just give up and confess.

462
00:29:54,022 --> 00:29:55,899
It's the least you can do

463
00:29:56,566 --> 00:29:58,360
to lessen the burden on others.

464
00:30:01,279 --> 00:30:02,656
What did you just say to me?

465
00:30:04,866 --> 00:30:05,742
Hey.

466
00:30:06,201 --> 00:30:06,868
Damn it.

467
00:30:07,786 --> 00:30:08,995
Can't you shut that mouth of yours?

468
00:30:10,580 --> 00:30:11,832
You want to kill me too?

469
00:30:14,334 --> 00:30:16,044
But can you really do it?

470
00:30:19,798 --> 00:30:22,467
Know your place, you loser.

471
00:30:23,844 --> 00:30:24,886
This bastard.

472
00:30:52,372 --> 00:30:53,707
Put in a little more effort.

473
00:31:19,316 --> 00:31:20,275
Oh.

474
00:31:52,265 --> 00:31:53,433
What's this?

475
00:31:54,476 --> 00:31:55,810
What are you doing here?

476
00:32:01,983 --> 00:32:03,151
You just press whatever?

477
00:32:04,486 --> 00:32:05,946
How did you even find me here?

478
00:32:08,406 --> 00:32:11,117
Do you know what happens
when a mouse is stressed?

479
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:14,370
You put one mouse in a glass box
and give it electric shocks periodically.

480
00:32:14,371 --> 00:32:16,248
Just little shocks, though.

481
00:32:16,957 --> 00:32:19,000
Prickled over and over.

482
00:32:20,460 --> 00:32:22,836
But even with a small shock,
over time,

483
00:32:22,837 --> 00:32:25,257
the mouse got cancer from the stress.

484
00:32:27,509 --> 00:32:29,386
What are you talking about? What stress?

485
00:32:29,636 --> 00:32:31,637
Now let's take two mice
and put them in the same box

486
00:32:31,638 --> 00:32:33,306
and give them the same electric shocks.

487
00:32:33,557 --> 00:32:35,225
What do you think will happen?

488
00:32:36,476 --> 00:32:37,978
Tell me. What do you think will happen?

489
00:32:40,272 --> 00:32:41,147
I don't know.

490
00:32:41,648 --> 00:32:43,567
The mice start fighting each other.

491
00:32:44,818 --> 00:32:46,194
But here's the funny part.

492
00:32:47,070 --> 00:32:49,573
While fighting,
they actually get healthier.

493
00:32:50,407 --> 00:32:52,158
Their fur shines,

494
00:32:53,034 --> 00:32:54,452
and their appetites become huge,

495
00:32:55,787 --> 00:32:57,497
while getting shocked,

496
00:32:58,373 --> 00:32:59,874
even though they get stressed.

497
00:33:00,959 --> 00:33:01,960
Interesting, right?

498
00:33:03,253 --> 00:33:04,796
What's so funny about that?

499
00:33:05,046 --> 00:33:08,675
The pain that doesn't kill me
makes me stronger.

500
00:33:11,886 --> 00:33:12,971
You didn't know?

501
00:33:13,638 --> 00:33:15,473
I guess we're meant to be.

502
00:33:16,266 --> 00:33:17,309
See you again.

503
00:33:25,650 --> 00:33:27,944
What's with her?

504
00:33:28,778 --> 00:33:30,488
HAN-MAUM BUILDING

505
00:33:34,200 --> 00:33:35,076
Hee-ju!

506
00:33:35,619 --> 00:33:37,286
Oh, Mr. Kim!

507
00:33:37,287 --> 00:33:39,163
Hello!

508
00:33:39,164 --> 00:33:40,790
I can get the contract ready right away.

509
00:33:42,042 --> 00:33:43,585
Sell the building.

510
00:33:43,835 --> 00:33:44,836
Not happening.

511
00:33:46,046 --> 00:33:47,255
Mr. Kim!

512
00:33:51,468 --> 00:33:53,553
What should we do?

513
00:33:54,095 --> 00:33:55,513
He's so stubborn.

514
00:33:56,765 --> 00:33:58,432
LAST WILL

515
00:33:58,433 --> 00:33:59,601
Your mother

516
00:34:00,352 --> 00:34:02,354
left all of her inheritance to you.

517
00:34:08,818 --> 00:34:09,653
This is

518
00:34:10,987 --> 00:34:13,073
the last business
she worked on while alive.

519
00:34:13,782 --> 00:34:14,615
SEJEONG-RO GLOBAL REDEVELOPMENT PROJECT

520
00:34:14,616 --> 00:34:16,325
The redevelopment area has changed...

521
00:34:16,326 --> 00:34:17,285
I get it.

522
00:34:20,538 --> 00:34:21,373
And this...

523
00:34:22,123 --> 00:34:23,625
I'm not sure what it is either.

524
00:34:26,336 --> 00:34:27,920
But your mother

525
00:34:27,921 --> 00:34:29,381
said it was her most treasured thing.

526
00:34:48,400 --> 00:34:50,193
I don't have a dad.

527
00:34:50,735 --> 00:34:52,904
Other kids have dads...

528
00:34:53,530 --> 00:34:56,157
It's just me
and my mom at our home.

529
00:34:57,033 --> 00:34:59,369
When I grow up, I'll be a mom.

530
00:35:00,036 --> 00:35:01,538
A mom just like my mom.

531
00:35:12,966 --> 00:35:14,925
I'll stop here for today.

532
00:35:14,926 --> 00:35:16,802
Please continue.

533
00:35:16,803 --> 00:35:18,471
I'm okay with it.

534
00:35:38,199 --> 00:35:39,200
Come in.

535
00:35:47,333 --> 00:35:48,293
Please have a seat.

536
00:35:50,670 --> 00:35:52,046
You're good at finding people, right?

537
00:35:53,173 --> 00:35:54,089
That's my specialty.

538
00:35:54,090 --> 00:35:55,091
I'm looking for that person.

539
00:35:55,467 --> 00:35:56,468
Who?

540
00:35:57,093 --> 00:35:58,970
Oh, the cafe owner?

541
00:36:00,305 --> 00:36:01,263
Yes.

542
00:36:01,264 --> 00:36:04,892
Hmm, if you have
any official documents related to him,

543
00:36:04,893 --> 00:36:05,977
it would make things easier.

544
00:36:07,979 --> 00:36:08,938
I'll get in touch.

545
00:36:10,231 --> 00:36:11,107
If we find him,

546
00:36:11,649 --> 00:36:12,734
shall we hand him over to the police?

547
00:36:17,989 --> 00:36:19,407
Oh, we can do anything

548
00:36:20,867 --> 00:36:21,868
as long as we get paid.

549
00:37:01,950 --> 00:37:03,033
Honey!

550
00:37:03,034 --> 00:37:04,244
Wake up!

551
00:37:04,661 --> 00:37:05,369
Huh?

552
00:37:05,370 --> 00:37:06,287
It's Yi-gyeong.

553
00:37:08,915 --> 00:37:10,792
Answer it, answer it.

554
00:37:15,964 --> 00:37:17,423
Hello, Yi-gyeong?

555
00:37:18,716 --> 00:37:19,883
Oh, Seon,

556
00:37:19,884 --> 00:37:21,343
I'm sorry for calling so late.

557
00:37:21,344 --> 00:37:23,303
Oh, no need to apologize.

558
00:37:23,304 --> 00:37:24,680
Did something happen?

559
00:37:24,681 --> 00:37:26,599
Oh, it's nothing serious.

560
00:37:27,892 --> 00:37:29,852
It's just that something happened
at your building,

561
00:37:29,853 --> 00:37:31,521
so I feel a bit bad.

562
00:37:32,856 --> 00:37:34,065
During the funeral,

563
00:37:34,732 --> 00:37:37,276
I was a bit out of it
and didn't speak much.

564
00:37:37,277 --> 00:37:39,278
What do you mean by that?

565
00:37:39,279 --> 00:37:41,281
You're the one who suffered.

566
00:37:41,739 --> 00:37:43,283
We're the ones who feel sorry.

567
00:37:48,496 --> 00:37:49,497
Yi-gyeong?

568
00:37:50,540 --> 00:37:51,541
Seon.

569
00:37:53,585 --> 00:37:55,128
Can you help me out?

570
00:37:57,171 --> 00:38:00,008
I'm having trouble
summarizing things.

571
00:38:00,466 --> 00:38:02,176
What did Yi-gyeong say?

572
00:38:02,343 --> 00:38:05,221
She sent someone
to personally find Oh Dong-ki.

573
00:38:05,805 --> 00:38:07,849
What is she going to do
once she finds him?

574
00:38:09,392 --> 00:38:10,643
Do I even need to say?

575
00:38:16,316 --> 00:38:18,609
We should give her the paperwork

576
00:38:18,610 --> 00:38:21,946
from the contract with Oh Dong-ki
that she asked for, right?

577
00:38:28,536 --> 00:38:29,704
Did you hear what I said?

578
00:38:32,081 --> 00:38:32,999
Seon.

579
00:38:33,291 --> 00:38:34,000
What?

580
00:38:35,835 --> 00:38:37,502
Do you see me

581
00:38:37,503 --> 00:38:38,421
as a loser too?

582
00:38:39,464 --> 00:38:41,007
Where's this coming from?

583
00:38:50,016 --> 00:38:51,809
What's going on with you two?

584
00:38:53,144 --> 00:38:54,312
Why are you still awake?

585
00:38:55,355 --> 00:38:57,482
Mom, Dad, what are you doing still up?

586
00:38:58,608 --> 00:38:59,441
Da-rae.

587
00:38:59,442 --> 00:39:02,612
Mom and Dad have a lot on their minds.

588
00:39:04,113 --> 00:39:06,866
What's on your mind?

589
00:39:08,743 --> 00:39:09,994
It's hard to explain.

590
00:39:10,912 --> 00:39:14,123
You'll understand when you grow up.

591
00:39:19,295 --> 00:39:22,422
Oh, right.
Aunt Yi-gyeong texted.

592
00:39:22,423 --> 00:39:25,593
She wants to go shopping this weekend.

593
00:39:31,808 --> 00:39:32,517
Seon.

594
00:39:34,727 --> 00:39:35,728
Just trust me this one time.

595
00:39:40,775 --> 00:39:42,652
What exactly do you want to do?

596
00:39:43,653 --> 00:39:45,279
You don't have to worry.

597
00:39:45,697 --> 00:39:46,781
I'll do it right this time.

598
00:39:47,323 --> 00:39:49,534
Well, I'm not really breaking the law.

599
00:39:49,909 --> 00:39:51,452
But why do I feel anxious?

600
00:39:52,161 --> 00:39:52,996
Seon.

601
00:39:54,038 --> 00:39:55,748
I really do want to change.

602
00:39:57,500 --> 00:39:58,918
I'll make it happen for sure.

603
00:39:59,669 --> 00:40:01,504
You just need to help a little.

604
00:40:03,047 --> 00:40:05,425
You're not someone
who can change so easily.

605
00:40:13,141 --> 00:40:14,808
What about the money?

606
00:40:14,809 --> 00:40:15,685
Is it ready?

607
00:40:23,401 --> 00:40:26,904
APRIL 3, BUGWANG SKYROAD

608
00:40:29,574 --> 00:40:30,366
Hey.

609
00:40:31,242 --> 00:40:32,743
I'm saying it again.

610
00:40:32,744 --> 00:40:34,871
If you pull any more nonsense,
I'll expose everything.

611
00:40:45,673 --> 00:40:46,590
Honey.

612
00:40:46,591 --> 00:40:47,674
I brought the documents.

613
00:40:47,675 --> 00:40:48,592
Okay.

614
00:40:48,593 --> 00:40:50,260
Put it on the table there.

615
00:40:50,261 --> 00:40:51,763
Oh, what's this?

616
00:40:53,931 --> 00:40:56,392
Wow, it's so milky white.
This will be revitalizing.

617
00:40:56,976 --> 00:40:58,352
The living has to live, right?

618
00:41:00,438 --> 00:41:01,605
Give it a taste.

619
00:41:01,606 --> 00:41:02,356
Okay.

620
00:41:03,399 --> 00:41:04,233
It's hot.

621
00:41:07,487 --> 00:41:09,071
Wow, it's really rich.

622
00:41:09,072 --> 00:41:09,654
It's so delicious.

623
00:41:09,655 --> 00:41:11,032
- It's good?
- Yes.

624
00:41:23,419 --> 00:41:24,545
Here you go.

625
00:41:25,838 --> 00:41:27,131
Thanks, Seon.

626
00:41:28,007 --> 00:41:28,883
You didn't have to.

627
00:41:30,635 --> 00:41:32,512
In times like this,
you need to eat well.

628
00:41:35,014 --> 00:41:37,433
My mom used
to really love gomtang too.

629
00:41:49,112 --> 00:41:50,196
It's delicious.

630
00:41:54,283 --> 00:41:57,870
Oh, you brought
what I asked for, right?

631
00:41:58,162 --> 00:41:59,288
Yes.

632
00:42:01,958 --> 00:42:02,875
Here you go.

633
00:42:08,005 --> 00:42:10,925
OH DONG-KI

634
00:42:15,388 --> 00:42:16,806
CAFE SINCERITY

635
00:42:29,110 --> 00:42:31,154
Loan Heaven / Will you hand me
the documents today?

636
00:42:34,407 --> 00:42:35,575
By the way, Yi-gyeong,

637
00:42:36,701 --> 00:42:37,660
are you okay?

638
00:42:39,036 --> 00:42:40,163
I'm fine.

639
00:42:41,414 --> 00:42:42,874
I'm not alone anymore.

640
00:42:45,001 --> 00:42:46,127
I'll think of my baby

641
00:42:47,461 --> 00:42:50,006
as the last gift my mom gave me.

642
00:42:51,799 --> 00:42:53,509
I'm going to start over again.

643
00:42:56,429 --> 00:42:59,307
If you need help, just let me know.

644
00:43:00,933 --> 00:43:01,934
Sure.

645
00:43:02,476 --> 00:43:06,314
But, I have a question.

646
00:43:06,939 --> 00:43:08,816
It's about Han-maum Building.

647
00:43:29,337 --> 00:43:32,840
Under investigation
No entry for those not involved

648
00:43:45,770 --> 00:43:46,937
Yes, Hee-su?

649
00:43:46,938 --> 00:43:48,147
Mr. Gi?

650
00:43:48,648 --> 00:43:50,732
I got a call from Han-maum.

651
00:43:50,733 --> 00:43:53,361
They want to meet tomorrow.
What's that about?

652
00:43:53,736 --> 00:43:56,614
Oh, I'll explain when we meet tomorrow.

653
00:43:57,073 --> 00:43:59,033
Just make sure
to prepare the contract well.

654
00:44:00,326 --> 00:44:01,118
Okay.

655
00:44:29,438 --> 00:44:31,232
I'll take Room 605 for my stay.

656
00:44:31,440 --> 00:44:32,525
That will be 50,000 won.

657
00:45:47,767 --> 00:45:48,768
Taxi!

658
00:46:08,371 --> 00:46:09,288
Ju-ran!

659
00:46:10,206 --> 00:46:11,123
Ju-ran!

660
00:46:12,208 --> 00:46:13,084
Ju-ran!

661
00:46:13,626 --> 00:46:14,543
Ju-ran!

662
00:47:15,271 --> 00:47:17,481
SEON: HE LEFT JUST NOW

663
00:47:44,633 --> 00:47:48,220
COME TO GYEONGWON-RO BELLUNA MOTEL

664
00:49:01,001 --> 00:49:04,046
DETECTIVE YOON BO-RAM: I'M ON MY WAY

665
00:49:34,868 --> 00:49:35,911
Police department.

666
00:49:36,328 --> 00:49:38,663
We're currently investigating.

667
00:49:38,664 --> 00:49:40,207
A man with a black hat
just went in, right?

668
00:49:42,585 --> 00:49:43,836
Do you know which room he is in?

669
00:49:44,378 --> 00:49:45,671
Room 606.

670
00:49:46,505 --> 00:49:47,715
Please give me the master key.

671
00:50:03,230 --> 00:50:04,273
WATCH YOUR STEP

672
00:52:10,441 --> 00:52:12,484
Yes, come to Room 606.

673
00:52:40,471 --> 00:52:41,596
OH DONG-KI

674
00:52:41,597 --> 00:52:42,848
This is Oh Dong-ki's room.

675
00:52:47,644 --> 00:52:48,604
What is this?

676
00:52:48,812 --> 00:52:49,937
Ju-ran.

677
00:52:49,938 --> 00:52:51,482
There are a lot of syringes
and strange stuff here.

678
00:53:01,450 --> 00:53:02,868
April 3, Bugwang Skyroad parking lot,
11:30 PM

679
00:53:06,121 --> 00:53:07,663
- Bo-ram.
- Yes?

680
00:53:07,664 --> 00:53:08,540
Look at this.

681
00:53:11,376 --> 00:53:12,084
April 3, Bugwang Skyroad parking lot,
11:30 PM

682
00:53:12,085 --> 00:53:12,711
What time is it now?

683
00:53:15,964 --> 00:53:16,840
It's now.

684
00:53:29,394 --> 00:53:30,561
Driver.

685
00:53:30,562 --> 00:53:32,564
Please hurry to Bugwang Skyroad.

686
00:53:46,787 --> 00:53:48,580
LOAN HEAVEN

687
00:53:53,585 --> 00:53:54,503
Hello?

688
00:53:55,754 --> 00:53:57,172
Are you looking for Oh Dong-ki?

689
00:54:11,311 --> 00:54:13,814
Damn it, why isn't he here?

690
00:54:27,870 --> 00:54:29,121
You didn't bring anyone, right?

691
00:54:29,496 --> 00:54:30,664
We'll all end up dying.

692
00:54:31,290 --> 00:54:32,291
No.

693
00:54:32,833 --> 00:54:33,834
Let's wrap this up fast.

694
00:54:34,585 --> 00:54:35,419
Where's the money?

695
00:54:37,462 --> 00:54:39,006
Quit joking around.

696
00:54:45,178 --> 00:54:46,096
Open it.

697
00:54:47,014 --> 00:54:47,973
Right here?

698
00:54:48,390 --> 00:54:49,766
Yes, right here and right now.

699
00:54:58,400 --> 00:54:59,234
Jeez.

700
00:55:02,529 --> 00:55:03,739
Hey, what are you doing?

701
00:55:10,120 --> 00:55:11,288
It's so simple.

702
00:55:37,105 --> 00:55:38,481
Seriously

703
00:55:38,482 --> 00:55:40,901
Thanks for keeping your promise
till the end.

704
00:55:42,069 --> 00:55:42,945
Sure.

705
00:55:46,365 --> 00:55:47,407
Damn it!

706
00:55:48,951 --> 00:55:50,243
It's fake, you bastard!

707
00:55:51,745 --> 00:55:53,413
You tried to fool me?

708
00:56:00,879 --> 00:56:02,005
Damn it!

709
00:56:05,300 --> 00:56:05,884
LOAN HEAVEN

710
00:56:10,764 --> 00:56:12,307
What's going on?

711
00:56:18,855 --> 00:56:19,605
Damn!

712
00:56:19,606 --> 00:56:20,273
What is this?

713
00:56:21,108 --> 00:56:22,233
Huh?

714
00:56:22,234 --> 00:56:23,067
- Let's go.
- Huh?

715
00:56:23,068 --> 00:56:25,028
Wait! Why me?

716
00:56:28,657 --> 00:56:29,908
Aren't we too late?

717
00:56:32,035 --> 00:56:33,536
Hold on!

718
00:56:33,537 --> 00:56:34,705
Damn it, this bastard!

719
00:56:38,208 --> 00:56:39,376
What's that?

720
00:56:39,876 --> 00:56:40,794
Block it for now.

721
00:56:49,386 --> 00:56:50,262
Damn!

722
00:56:52,764 --> 00:56:53,598
Grab him!

723
00:56:57,894 --> 00:56:58,979
- Come here!
- No!

724
00:57:00,814 --> 00:57:01,940
Don't move!

725
00:57:16,455 --> 00:57:17,372
Damn!

726
00:57:17,706 --> 00:57:18,623
You!

727
00:57:19,499 --> 00:57:20,333
Yoon Bo-ram!

728
00:57:34,181 --> 00:57:35,139
Don't come any closer!

729
00:57:35,140 --> 00:57:36,558
Any closer and I'll kill him!

730
00:57:41,521 --> 00:57:42,481
Drop the gun.

731
00:57:43,398 --> 00:57:44,274
Who do you think you are?

732
00:57:44,733 --> 00:57:45,400
Put the gun down!

733
00:57:46,902 --> 00:57:48,194
Drop the gun or I'll really shoot!

734
00:57:48,195 --> 00:57:49,321
I said put it down!

735
00:57:50,739 --> 00:57:51,740
Drop the gun!

736
00:57:52,240 --> 00:57:53,825
I said put it down
or I'll shoot!

737
00:58:06,671 --> 00:58:07,380
Damn it.

738
00:58:30,195 --> 00:58:31,363
What are you doing?
Pick up the gun!

739
00:58:35,033 --> 00:58:35,951
Damn.

740
00:59:17,659 --> 00:59:18,577
Hello?

741
00:59:19,411 --> 00:59:20,745
Oh Dong-ki is dead.

742
00:59:23,123 --> 00:59:24,082
He's dead?

743
00:59:24,374 --> 00:59:25,709
The police shot him.

744
00:59:25,917 --> 00:59:27,002
The police?

745
00:59:32,924 --> 00:59:33,758
Yes.

746
00:59:34,301 --> 00:59:35,759
I brought two billion

747
00:59:35,760 --> 00:59:36,678
in cash.

748
00:59:39,347 --> 00:59:40,973
Yi-gyeong

749
00:59:40,974 --> 00:59:43,393
says good things about your family.

750
00:59:43,852 --> 00:59:45,061
Oh, I see.

751
00:59:47,606 --> 00:59:50,358
Just because you have a lot
doesn't mean you're happy.

752
00:59:52,152 --> 00:59:52,903
Yes.

753
00:59:54,446 --> 00:59:55,863
Our family

754
00:59:55,864 --> 00:59:58,033
just needs to have enough
to take care of ourselves.

755
00:59:58,450 --> 01:00:00,243
Don't you already have that much?

756
01:00:00,785 --> 01:00:02,661
It'll be just this much.

757
01:00:02,662 --> 01:00:04,331
Your building will be the last one.

758
01:00:20,222 --> 01:00:21,723
Are you sure you can stop?

759
01:00:22,849 --> 01:00:24,226
What do you mean?

760
01:00:25,101 --> 01:00:27,354
Not giving up takes courage,

761
01:00:28,647 --> 01:00:29,980
but when the time comes,

762
01:00:29,981 --> 01:00:31,983
knowing when to stop also takes courage.

763
01:00:33,276 --> 01:00:34,736
Keep this in mind

764
01:00:36,571 --> 01:00:37,864
for Da-rae's sake.

765
01:00:40,033 --> 01:00:41,117
Yes, I understand.

766
01:00:58,093 --> 01:00:58,969
Yes.

767
01:01:10,689 --> 01:01:12,524
Take good care of Yi-gyeong.

768
01:01:13,191 --> 01:01:15,318
She's a special girl to me.

769
01:01:17,362 --> 01:01:18,363
I will.

770
01:01:29,082 --> 01:01:30,332
Congratulations!

771
01:01:30,333 --> 01:01:31,875
You really hit the jackpot at 30 billion!

772
01:01:31,876 --> 01:01:33,544
This is all thanks to you, Hee-ju.

773
01:01:33,545 --> 01:01:35,546
So, am I getting a bonus?

774
01:01:35,547 --> 01:01:37,173
Oh, absolutely.
Let's talk about it outside.

775
01:01:51,313 --> 01:01:52,272
Da-rae,

776
01:01:52,605 --> 01:01:55,734
pick something better, okay?

777
01:01:58,903 --> 01:02:00,404
It's too expensive.

778
01:02:00,405 --> 01:02:01,947
Oh, it's fine.

779
01:02:01,948 --> 01:02:02,866
It's fine.

780
01:02:03,366 --> 01:02:04,575
Excuse me.

781
01:02:04,576 --> 01:02:05,368
Yes?

782
01:02:06,244 --> 01:02:08,370
I'd like
to get this wrapped up.

783
01:02:08,371 --> 01:02:09,581
Sure, I'll take care of that.

784
01:02:11,499 --> 01:02:13,083
Thank you.

785
01:02:13,084 --> 01:02:14,127
It's okay.

786
01:02:15,420 --> 01:02:16,588
- Shall we look around more?
- Sure.

787
01:02:30,143 --> 01:02:32,228
I got a call
from the detective.

788
01:02:32,812 --> 01:02:35,815
They said your tenant was the kidnapper.

789
01:02:38,443 --> 01:02:40,069
Mom, I'll be right back.

790
01:02:40,070 --> 01:02:41,321
Okay, go ahead.

791
01:02:44,532 --> 01:02:46,493
Why would he do
something like that?

792
01:02:47,952 --> 01:02:48,828
For money?

793
01:02:50,205 --> 01:02:52,499
I'm not sure. Well,

794
01:02:53,541 --> 01:02:56,168
it's a world
where people betray friends

795
01:02:56,169 --> 01:02:58,004
and kill their families for money.

796
01:03:00,715 --> 01:03:02,550
All for just three billion won?

797
01:03:04,552 --> 01:03:06,805
Humans are truly pathetic, aren't they?

798
01:03:09,307 --> 01:03:10,934
Don't betray me, Seon.

799
01:03:11,518 --> 01:03:13,561
I could easily
give you three billion won.

800
01:03:20,944 --> 01:03:22,444
Oh my!

801
01:03:22,445 --> 01:03:23,988
I guess it's time for morning sickness.

802
01:03:24,280 --> 01:03:25,865
- Are you okay?
- I'm fine.

803
01:03:26,908 --> 01:03:30,912
Try a morning sickness shot.
It'll help supply nutrition for you too.

804
01:03:31,788 --> 01:03:33,705
Do you know
a place that's good?

805
01:03:33,706 --> 01:03:35,542
Let me introduce you
to a hospital I know.

806
01:03:37,836 --> 01:03:40,546
Just go there and ask for the head nurse.

807
01:03:40,547 --> 01:03:42,339
If you say I'm your friend,
they'll treat you well.

808
01:03:42,340 --> 01:03:44,050
There is no one like you.

809
01:03:47,095 --> 01:03:49,597
YEON HWA-JIN INTERNAL MEDICINE

810
01:03:52,684 --> 01:03:53,934
Head nurse at Yeon Hwa-jin Medicine:
Have you made the deposit?

811
01:03:53,935 --> 01:03:54,811
DEPOSIT COMPLETED

812
01:04:01,192 --> 01:04:02,193
Do you like it?

813
01:04:39,314 --> 01:04:43,818
FOR RENT

814
01:05:00,668 --> 01:05:01,836
Good job.

815
01:05:02,170 --> 01:05:03,838
I have a good eye for people.

816
01:05:06,424 --> 01:05:08,051
I'll do better from now on.

817
01:05:17,477 --> 01:05:19,979
I didn't see this coming.

818
01:05:31,491 --> 01:05:32,116
Hey.

819
01:05:40,833 --> 01:05:41,751
Are you happy?

820
01:06:13,449 --> 01:06:16,493
MAD CONCRETE DREAMS

821
01:06:16,494 --> 01:06:18,579
Check in at Pyeong-buk Gwan.

822
01:06:18,580 --> 01:06:20,747
I want to check
if it's the same drug that was used

823
01:06:20,748 --> 01:06:22,499
when I was kidnapped.

824
01:06:22,500 --> 01:06:24,084
What did you whisper earlier?

825
01:06:24,085 --> 01:06:26,420
Living like this
feels like hell, even now.

826
01:06:26,421 --> 01:06:28,339
So, stop bothering me.

827
01:06:28,506 --> 01:06:29,756
It feels good
to wake up, right?

828
01:06:29,757 --> 01:06:32,468
I need your signature
for asset inheritance.

